@prefix backlog: <http://example.org/backlog#> .
@prefix ex:      <http://example.org/sen0414-ch18corr-lineage#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch18corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapter 18 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch18corr-lineage/1.0.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch18corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.0.0 (2026-11-18): Mission stage only (one stage per version). Opened on the owner's instructions of 2026-11-15 (correct the earlier chapters as urgency, after Lineage8) and 2026-11-18 ('Yes, first the corrections. We want to reduce the rework.').
ORDINAL AND ONE-AT-A-TIME CHECK: the latest version of every lineage file was read; Lineage8 (chapters 19-20) was closed LS_Achieved on 2026-11-18 (register v1_19_0, commit pushed) before this lineage opened, so only this lineage runs. Lineage3 (ch9-10) still has one carried-forward item, a pre-existing state reported earlier and not changed here. The next free ordinal is 9.
VERIFIED GAPS (live files measured 2026-11-18 with cme_material_check v1.0.1 on deck v2_0_3 and page v9_96_2, not memory): 49 of 53 slide notes outside 60 to 140 words; 3 of 41 titles under 4 words; 1 of 41 content slides without one thing to look at; 120 of 175 code checks carry a prompt marker (the deck builder prints a '>>> ' before every line); 112 of 128 code frames do not parse as shown; 36 of 128 slide code frames are not found in the page; 322 lambda occurrences in the page code; no Slide code tab; the story layout is labelled (WHO/WHAT/WHEN prefixes). Source of the rulings: 09-handovers-out/HANDOVER_session_to_next-session_deck-and-page-rulings_v1_1_0.md (owner, 2026-11-14).
WHY A NEW LINEAGE: Lineage8 is closed and a closed lineage is revived only in extraordinary cases; the owner asked for corrections as a new piece of work, and chapter 18 is a different slice from chapters 19-20.
REDUCING REWORK (owner, 2026-11-18): the deck is rebuilt once through the generic chapter builder that chapters 19-20 now use (the chapter's examples, visuals and words moved into a spec; notes written once), instead of patching frames one by one; the page is rebuilt through the same maker and test that chapters 19-20 passed. The conversion tool stays reusable for chapters 17 and earlier."""@en .

ex:ProfileDecl9 a backlog:ProfileDeclaration ;
    rdfs:label "Profile: AAL (agentic adaptive), default"@en ;
    backlog:declaresProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:declaresLevel backlog:Level_L2 ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_Default ;
    backlog:hasDeclarationRationale "Same declaration as Lineage3 to Lineage8: work is executed by an LLM agent, no human team; AAL is the default profile for agent-executed work. Level L2 stated plainly." ;
    backlog:declaredAt "2026-11-18T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:reviewDate "2026-11-25"^^xsd:date .

ex:Lineage9 a backlog:Lineage ;
    rdfs:label "Chapter 18 corrections, narrow lineage"@en ;
    backlog:lineageForMission ex:Mission9 ; backlog:lineageOrdinal 9 ; backlog:lineageArchived false ;
    backlog:hasLineageStatus backlog:LS_Opened ;
    backlog:hasProfile backlog:Profile_AAL ; backlog:followsProfileDeclaration ex:ProfileDecl9 ;
    backlog:continuesFrom ex:Lineage2 ;
    rdfs:comment "ex:Lineage2 (sen0414-slides-lineage namespace) is the closed slides lineage this continues from, as Lineage3 to Lineage8 do."@en .

ex:Mission9 a backlog:Mission ;
    rdfs:label "Chapter 18 deck and page meet the owner's rulings of 2026-11-14"@en ;
    backlog:missionFor ex:Backlog9 ;
    backlog:hasMissionStatement "The chapter 18 (CSV, JSON and XML Files) deck and interactive page, already released, are corrected so that they meet the six rulings of 2026-11-14 on decks and pages (one thing taught per slide, notes that carry the lecture, a Slide code tab, plain code without prompts, only taught Python, checks and reviews recorded before release), with the chapter's approved content, stories and examples unchanged, and with the correction made through a conversion that later chapters can reuse." ;
    backlog:hasMissionOrigin "Owner's instruction 2026-11-15 (correct the chapters of the past and next week as urgency, after the running lineage) and 2026-11-18 ('first the corrections; reduce the rework')." .
